# =============================================================================
# .gitattributes — line-ending policy
#
# Every tracked file in this repo is text, and all of it is LF.
#   text=auto  → git detects text and normalises it to LF in the index on commit
#   eol=lf     → git checks it out as LF in the working tree, on every platform
#
# Why this exists. CRLF drifted in repeatedly and invisibly:
#   * config.fish was wholly CRLF while the rest of the repo was LF, and edits
#     left it mixed                                          (fixed in 9839609)
#   * README.md picked up mixed endings three separate times in one branch
#     series — twice merged before anyone noticed             (fixed in 2ed5141)
#   * starship.toml was the last holdout                      (fixed in #8)
#
# Mixed endings don't show up in a normal diff, and they turn a one-line edit
# into a whole-file rewrite that buries the real change. Cheaper to prevent.
#
# Verified at the time of adding: no binary files are tracked. If one is ever
# added, exempt it explicitly so git never rewrites its bytes, e.g.:
#     *.png binary
#     *.icns binary
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf
